# Title: ETW Trace Evasion Activity
# ID: a238b5d0-ce2d-4414-a676-7a531b3d13d6
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: @neu5ron, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
# Date: 2019-03-22
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1070, attack.t1685, car.2016-04-002
# Description: Detects command line activity that tries to clear or disable any ETW trace log which could be a sign of logging evasion.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((CommandLine CONTAIN "cl" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "/Trace")) OR ((CommandLine CONTAIN "clear-log" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "/Trace")) OR ((CommandLine CONTAIN "sl" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "/e:false")) OR ((CommandLine CONTAIN "set-log" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "/e:false")) OR ((CommandLine CONTAIN "logman" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "update" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "trace" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "--p" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "-ets")) OR (CommandLine CONTAIN "Remove-EtwTraceProvider") OR ((CommandLine CONTAIN "Set-EtwTraceProvider" AND CommandLine CONTAIN "0x11")))
